          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of totally convex spaces is essentially what one obtains when formulating an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theory"} algebraic theory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+spaces"} Banach spaces
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          #slick.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p (abstractly)
            %p
              A
              %strong totally convex space
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+for+a+monad"} module
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              which sends a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+ball"} closed unit ball
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+space"} Banach space
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell^1(X)
          %p
            This is an example of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theory"} algebraic theory
            (in the strong sense that it is
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+category"} bounded monadic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free
            totally convex space on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the unit ball of the Banach space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell^1(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi x
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{x \in X} a_x x
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_x \in \mathbb{R}
            with the property that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{x \in X} {|a_x|} \le 1
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell^1(\mathbb{N})
            (which is why the theory is
            %em bounded
            monadic). The corresponding identities are simply the substitution rules – namely that substituting a sum into another works as expected – and the reordering rules.
          #concrete.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p (concretely)
            %p
              A
              %strong totally convex space
              is a non-empty set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              equipped with, for each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+sequence"} infinite sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1, a_2, \ldots)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_i {|a_i|} \leq 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{\mathbb{N}}
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↦
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_1,x_2,\ldots) \mapsto \sum_i a_i x_i
            %ol
              %li
                Reordering: If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                is any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permutation
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_i a_i x_i = \sum_i a_{\sigma(i)} x_{\sigma(i)}
              %li
                Nullary substitution: If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_i
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kronecker+delta"} Kronecker delta
                at
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                (so
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_i = 0
                normally, but
                = succeed ")," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mn 0
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_0 = 1
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_i \delta_i x_i = x_0
              %li
                Binary substitution: If the functions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi,\rho\colon \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}
                express
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
                as its own
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
                with itself (it is enough to pick one pair of functions and state this axiom only for it), then
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ,
                            %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ,
                            %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi k
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mrow
                            %mi π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mrow
                            %mi π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mrow
                            %mi π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_i a_i (\sum_j b_{i,j} x_{i,j}) = \sum_k a_{\pi(k)} b_{\pi(k),\rho(k)} x_{\pi(k),\rho(k)}
          %p
            Of course, one would normally write the right-hand side of the last equation as
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{i,j} a_i b_{i,j} x_{i,j}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi π
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\pi,\rho)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo +
                        %mi j
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i,j) \mapsto \big({i + j + 1 \atop 2}\big) + j
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            to be a natural number.
          %p
            A totally convex space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            has the same axioms as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+convex+space"} super convex space
            except that a totally convex space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            must be a nonempty set, and the condition for countable affine sums
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{i \in \mathbb{N}} a_i x_i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{i \in \mathbb{N}} |a_i| = 1
            for super convex spaces, is replaced by the inequality
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{i \in \mathbb{N}} |a_i|\le 1
          .query
            %p I haven't actually checked that this list is complete; but it's what I get if I take Andrew at his word that we need only substitution and reordering rules. I wouldn't be terribly surprised if nullary substitution is redundant, but right now I don't see how. —Toby
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                A totally convex space is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+space"} convex space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi r
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi r
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (r, 1 - r, 0, 0, 0, \ldots)
                and the “point” comes from the operation
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0, 0, \ldots)
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %li
              %p
                The operations for this theory are
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebraic+theory"} commutative
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                of totally convex spaces is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
                category.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Clearly, the closed unit ball
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B X
                of any Banach space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a totally convex space.
            %li
              %p
                Bizarrely, the
                %strong open
                unit ball of a Banach space is a totally convex space. This is because if a sum,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi B
                          %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi x
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{x \in B X} a_x x
                for
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi x
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_x {|a_x|} \leq 1
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B X
                then every
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                for which
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi x
                      %mo ≠
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_x \ne 0
                must have norm
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B X
                %span.newWikiWord
                  subalgebra
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/subalgebra"} ?
                of the closed unit ball.
            %li
              %p Continuing, the quotient of the closed unit ball by the open unit ball is a totally convex space.
            %li
              %p
                In particular, the three-point space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{-1,0,1\}
                is (assuming
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi j
                      %msub
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mrow
                          %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mn 1
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϵ
                                  %mi j
                                %mo =
                                %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} sign
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi a
                                  %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ,
                                %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mi j
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mo =
                                %mn 1
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϵ
                                  %mi j
                                %mo =
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} sign
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi a
                                  %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ,
                                %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mi j
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mo =
                                %mn 1
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mn 0
                              %mtd
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mtext otherwise
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\sum a_j \epsilon_j = \begin{cases}
                      1 &amp; \epsilon_j = \operatorname{sign}(a_j), \sum {|a_j|} = 1 \\
                      \-1 &amp; \epsilon_j = -\operatorname{sign}(a_j), \sum {|a_j|} = 1 \\
                      0 &amp; \;\text{otherwise}
                      \\end{cases}
            %li
              %p
                Going back one step,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1,1)
                is a totally convex space. It is illuminating to describe this as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequaliser"} coequaliser
                of free totally convex spaces. Consider a functional
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi ℓ
